A||||3||fix her up||Damn Suicidal Deer||||9||
Z||000000||fix her up||10-10-2001||01:43 PM||||Last Friday morning a suicidal deer chose my Gt to do it self in with. I'm running 60 MPH and all of a sudden a Deer is in front of me, then I am driving through deer and car parts debris. I didn't even have time to get my foot of the gas. I never got a scratch, but the GT sure was abused. <BR>  On the passenger side it sheared of my headlight, Broke my parking light, tore my mirror off and left it hanging by the wires, pushed the hood almost to the windshield and ripped it up when it got the headlight. It tore the top bolts out of my facia, messed up the facia paint and ripped my GT emblem of the front. Last but not least it cracked my windshield. She is still drive-able with one eye blind, and not so pretty any more. If I had been driving my Ranger, it would have hit the windshield and ended up in the front seat with me. You gotta love these cars fun and safe.<BR>  Here are my questions. Did some of the 87s use 88 style headlights? The ones in my 87 2M4 are like the earlier headlights, complete with relays. The ones on my GT have a smaller motor and no relays. Last are the hoods on all Fieros the same? I know the GT back decks are different. I took some preliminary measurements and they look the same to me. Thanks for your help in advance. I have been reading and learning from this forum for some time and it has been a life saver. When the 2M4 graces the road I will post it's adventure and lessons learned.<P>------------------<BR>87 Gold GT  Daily Driver<BR>87 Red 2M4 4 speed almost running<BR>84 Silver SE Parts and future project car||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||10-10-2001||02:16 PM||||Welcome to the Forum.<P>Yes..some of (I thought all of) the 87's use the same headlights as the 88's.  They are the same thing.<P>And yes...all Fiero hoods are the same.  <P>Hope that helps and good luck fixin the deer damage.  Stupid Deer.  Just glad you were not injured.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-10-2001||02:17 PM||||The hoods on all models are the same. Sounds like either you have the year wrong on the '2M4' as 87 & 88 use the same headlight motors and wiring. Either that or someone for some reason put an old harness w/motors in it. If you still have your headlight motor that was in the car to begin with, you can swap the bad housing out and swap motors.||||reg||1
Z||000003||montage||10-10-2001||02:28 PM||||One thing that I found works 99% of the time when I see a deer is beep the horn. It has saved my butt several times. I think the horn gives the deer some sense of direction of danger especially at night when they are overloaded with light from your headlights. The usually run the opposite direction I'm at instead running in front of me. ||||reg||1
